/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:177:Highlight black defects in blue foreground by surrounding them with orange.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:178:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:179:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:180:- Blue (1) foreground on black (0) bg; small black holes or protrusions within blue regions; occasional thin blue spurs into black areas.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:181:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:182:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:183:- Thin blue pixels mostly surrounded by black are absorbed into the background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:184:- Small black components (≤3 cells) and leaf pixels of larger black components are "defects."
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:185:- Each defect gets an orange (7) 8-neighbor halo; the defect pixels themselves stay black.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:186:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:187:Key insight: Only structural anomalies—tiny isolated patches and dangling endpoints—are marked, not bulk black regions.
