/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:228:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:229:Scale up a monochrome control sprite by stamping a polychrome tile at each filled pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:230:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:231:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:232:- bg = background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:233:- Two foreground objects (8-connected): a monochrome rectangular sprite with bg holes (control), and a polychrome square tile (block).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:234:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:235:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:236:- For each cell in the control sprite's bbox: if filled, stamp a copy of the block tile; if bg, leave a tile-sized bg region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:237:- Output grid dimensions are (control_h × tile_h) by (control_w × tile_w).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:238:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:239:Key insight: The control sprite acts as a binary mask that gets "pixel-scaled" by the tile — each pixel expands to a full tile copy or empty space.
