/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:245:Let the largest center-pointing object grow outward while every other object loses its inward tip.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:246:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:247:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:248:- The grid has a single dominant background color and four 8-connected monochromatic foreground objects.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:249:- The objects surround a central background gap and point toward it from cardinal directions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:250:- Exactly one object has the largest area.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:251:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:252:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:253:- Find the central background gap by minimizing aggregate distance to the four objects.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:254:- Recolor the nearest-to-center pixel of each non-largest object to background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:255:- Add a three-pixel cap in the largest object's color on the side away from the center, centered on the shared row or column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:256:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:257:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:258:- The edit is a transfer of prominence around a common center: losers retract at their tips, and the unique largest object extends outward from the center.
