/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:266:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:267:- bg = background. Non-bg cells form wire networks and 3×3 tokens (solid blocks or X/diagonal patterns) near wire endpoints.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:268:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:269:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:270:- Every solid 3×3 token is replaced in-place by a diamond (center + 4 cardinal neighbors).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:271:- Each token near a wire endpoint sends its complement to the opposite endpoint: solid emits X, X emits diamond.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:272:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:273:Key insight: Token shape cycles solid → X → diamond; wires route each complement to the far end.
