/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:280:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:281:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:282:- The background is the dominant color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:283:- Foreground components are made from a path color, a paired gate-end color, and single marker pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:284:- A gate is a straight end-center-end motif whose center has the path color and whose two ends share the gate-end color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:285:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:286:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:287:- In every 4-connected foreground component with exactly one marker and one gate, erase the marker and all path-color pixels except the gate center.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:288:- Place the marker on the unique path-color pixel adjacent to the gate center but not between the two gate ends.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:289:- Components without both a marker and a gate stay unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:290:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:291:Key insight: The black-green-black motif marks the stopping gate; the gray marker consumes the connected green path until it rests on the path cell immediately beside that gate.
