/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:377:Simulate particles along a path with alternating turn direction at collisions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:378:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:379:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:380:- Top-left: 2x2 monochrome blocks define a repeating color cycle (left-to-right).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:381:- Isolated single pixels of a cycle color: start markers adjacent to the path.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:382:- A 2x2 monochrome block of a distinct color: end marker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:383:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:384:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:385:- Each start marker launches a particle moving straight, painting cycle colors in order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:386:- On hitting a boundary, paint that cell with the end color and turn 90°.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:387:- Turn direction alternates: odd collisions → left (CCW), even → right (CW).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:388:- If the scheduled turn is blocked, the particle stops.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:389:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:390:Key insight: The alternating left/right turn rule is the core mechanism; without it the path would be trivial.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed287049989/11/prompt.md:391:</description>
